{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1785994246802686001,"compiled_state":{"alias":"sail-shoe-smear","assignee":"","attestations":{"plan-review":{"algorithm":"HMAC-SHA256","author":"Joe Oakhart","head_sha":"c698cd243a05f21eff6b14703961c9f500e0853f","key_id":"412fa5372ad877e0","kind":"plan-review","manifest":["plan-review: PASS","ticket: b02d-10bc-07ee-49e7","material: 6dbac97f88708527","model: claude-sonnet-4-6","runner: pydantic_ai","blocking: 0","advisory: 16","rebar-version: 0.6.0 (c698cd243)","regver: bb57585159a067c5","verified-at-sha:c698cd243a05f21eff6b14703961c9f500e0853f"],"signature":"63dae525021eb102c7090bf8022df138c397f9dcc022d0673d4fc61f5d77692d","signed_at":1783188581815689000}},"author":"Claude","authorship":{"signed":1,"unsigned":9},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"189fd21443da62b8a0896f4234f6889683fdb64e1b10f395f7ad73abc9df72b1","event_uuid":"4b8b5423-7aac-417e-9b67-00db5fcc972e","position":{"commit_sha":"e2aa6eee1c7a804b45c31064ea49de2235c5cdc7","position":"1785007223191249001-4b8b5423-7aac-417e-9b67-00db5fcc972e"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"Joe Oakhart","body":"STATUS (session pause, worktree .claude/worktrees/sail-shoe-smear, branch worktree-sail-shoe-smear, 5 commits ahead of origin/main c698cd243):\n\nCLOSED (5/10 children):\n- 3ee0 community health files — signed completion-verifier PASS (commit ed6dcfbb1)\n- b593 pyproject metadata — FORCE-CLOSED, uncertified (commit 2c1b2f403). Completion-verifier could not RUN: rebar-internal plumbing bug (verify model returns top-level JSON array; validate_to 'got list'), reproduced 5/5. Tracked as bug dash-lure-slag (discovered_from this epic). NOTE: because this child is closed-but-uncertified, the epic's own completion gate will read certifiable=false — re-close b593 cleanly (rebar reopen b593 then transition closed) once dash-lure-slag is fixed, OR accept an unsigned epic close.\n- e110 run_workflow durability docstrings — signed PASS (commit 3ed767d7c)\n- fce6 MCP ToolAnnotations on all 45 tools + mcp floor >=1.9 — signed PASS (commit a38b61fae)\n- b49a server.json env contract + MCP_ENV_VARS SoT + CI drift-guard — signed PASS (commit af2d2ee6a)\n\nOPEN (5/10 remaining): 95dc supply-chain CI (plan-review PASS already earned), 3a10 typed models, 830d api-stability doc, d063 scale-envelope doc, 3bf6 README quickstart. All plan-reviews returned PASS with 0 blocking; advisories triaged inline per commit.\n\nINFRA: tickets-branch auto-push has been failing (shared-remote merge conflicts) all session — local store is intact; run 'rebar fsck-recover' / reconcile before final landing.\n\nLANDING: not started. Multi-story epic -> per CONTRIBUTING.md landing goes through Gerrit (feature branch or single squash change).","timestamp":1783220309188133001},{"author":"Joe Oakhart","body":"LANDING (Gerrit §4): feature branch refs/heads/feature/oss-readiness created off gerrit/main (1b77c6da); rebased the 10 epic commits onto current gerrit/main (was 7 behind) — clean, tree re-verified green (typecheck 267 files, lint, 27 schema/types tests). Pushed the 10-commit chain for review as Gerrit changes 291-300. Awaiting LLM-Review + Verified on each, then submit bottom-up + a --no-ff merge-back change into main.","timestamp":1783268922713219001},{"author":"Joe Oakhart","body":"LANDED on main via Gerrit (§4). All 10 stories reviewed into feature/oss-readiness as changes 291-300 (each LLM-Review+1 AND Verified+1, zero blocks/CI failures; CI on the bottom of the chain needed a 'recheck' to trigger). Submitted the chain, then the single --no-ff merge-back (change 301: LLM-Review+1 merge-change over 10 integrated commits, Verified+1) submitted into main = merge commit 3af43180a. gerrit/main advanced 1b77c6da..3af43180a and replicates to the GitHub mirror. Epic complete.","timestamp":1783274453745552001}],"created_at":1783148760842271880,"creation_channel":"unknown","deps":[],"description":"## Context\n\nAn external architectural review graded rebar's engineering core near\n\"high-assurance internal platform\" quality (A-/B+ across architecture,\nconcurrency, CLI, MCP, CI) but its **public OSS/community packaging** a full tier\nlower (C+ community readiness, B docs, B library-API clarity). Every factual\nclaim in that review was verified against the tree: no `SECURITY.md` /\n`CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md` / issue+PR templates; `server.json` advertises only 3 env\nvars and the *deprecated* `REBAR_MCP_ALLOW_RECONCILE_LIVE`, omitting\n`REBAR_MCP_ALLOW_LLM` + `REBAR_MCP_ALLOW_JIRA_SYNC`; MCP tools carry no\nbehavior annotations; `pyproject` has no authors/keywords/classifiers/urls; no\nSAST / dependency-vuln scanning; no published API-stability policy or scale\nenvelope; the `run_workflow` docstring oversells a `daemon`-thread as\n\"resumable on crash\"; and the `rebar.*` facade returns bare dicts with no\ndocumented typed contract.\n\nThis epic closes the **OSS-surface gap only** — the packaging, community,\nmanifest-accuracy, docs, and library-contract layer — WITHOUT touching the\nfunctional/correctness roadmap already tracked in\n`docs/oss-comparison-and-remediation.md` (HLC ordering, authenticated identity,\ngit-gc growth). Scope was locked interactively with the maintainer; three heavy\nengineering items were deliberately excluded (see Scope · OUT).\n\n## Scope\n\n### IN (10 workstreams, decomposed into the child stories below)\n1. Community health files (SECURITY, CODE_OF_CONDUCT, issue/PR templates, SUPPORT).\n2. Fix `server.json` env/config contract + add a CI drift-guard.\n3. Annotate MCP tools with behavior hints.\n4. Enrich `pyproject` package metadata.\n5. Supply-chain CI hardening (CodeQL + pip-audit + alerts + attestation docs).\n6. API-stability matrix doc.\n7. Scale-envelope doc.\n8. External onboarding quickstart (single-sourced; defers to `rebar --help`).\n9. `run_workflow` durability-docstring honesty fix.\n10. Typed public library models (schema-derived TypedDicts, drift-gated).\n\n### OUT (explicitly deferred; not part of this epic)\n- **Durable workflow runner** (lease/reaper/resume worker) — separate effort;\n  only the docstring-honesty fix (WS9) is in scope here.\n- **Batched-commit bulk import** — touches the invariant-gated write path;\n  belongs with the functional-remediation plan.\n- **PR->Gerrit mirror bot** — ongoing service, contested vs. the Gerrit gate;\n  the redirect PR template (WS1) delivers the cheap substitute.\n- **OpenSSF Scorecard badge/workflow** — dropped: Code-Review/Branch-Protection\n  sub-scores read low BY DESIGN on a Gerrit-gated mirror.\n- **CI benchmark harness** and **SBOM** — deferred; docs-only scale envelope\n  (WS7) and CI-check-only supply chain (WS5) instead.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] All 10 in-scope workstreams are decomposed into child stories/tasks parented\n  to this epic, each with its own `## Acceptance Criteria`.\n- [ ] Each child ticket passes the plan-review gate (run in an LLM-enabled\n  environment) and, on completion, the completion-verifier gate.\n- [ ] No child ticket modifies the invariant-gated write path or introduces a\n  new runtime dependency into the deliberately-tiny core\n  (`pyyaml`/`jsonschema`/`referencing`); the typed-models work is static-only.\n- [ ] The OUT items above are NOT implemented under this epic.\n- [ ] `make lint` and the existing CI gates remain green after each child lands.\n- [ ] A newcomer landing on the GitHub mirror finds the standard community\n- [ ] The MCP `server.json` manifest matches the real config/env contract and is\n- [ ] MCP clients can render safe UI from tool behavior hints\n- [ ] `nava-rebar` presents complete, discoverable PyPI metadata (authors,\n- [ ] Supply-chain posture adds SAST (CodeQL) + dependency-vulnerability scanning\n- [ ] The public contract surface (CLI / JSON schemas / Python facade / MCP\n- [ ] An honest scale envelope (counts, throughput, latency, git-growth,\n- [ ] The `run_workflow` durability docstring states true crash semantics.\n- [ ] The `rebar.*` facade has a documented typed return contract (schema-derived","env_id":"58e9f32e-f999-436d-9c1a-5d0eef5c9903","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"a24d4f2e-9512-49e4-bbc2-80762339dc98","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"b02d-10bc-07ee-49e7","ticket_type":"epic","title":"OSS-readiness surface: community files, MCP manifest, packaging, docs, API contract","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["34e9a6e4-8fa4-431b-8a56-e689ea83167e","4fff5c50-f5ac-4bd2-94dc-3873132b3162","769f8fe0-6544-43c4-9e24-a86620c8fb01","9815ce96-9fc9-4cc4-a9bf-2340dc2c939e","a24d4f2e-9512-49e4-bbc2-80762339dc98","59392f87-140c-4a9d-bd49-ac864dd097e2","3e98b91b-07ae-4354-b429-fdf2a2125af6","e420cbd4-1857-4dde-9069-ab00d46df5c2","b34a3d17-be15-49e7-b984-20a17cd2a804","ee8b78ed-3c20-4bef-91c0-9b1f4bb8e757","4b8b5423-7aac-417e-9b67-00db5fcc972e"]},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1785994246802686001,"uuid":"75ec48b6-9163-4e41-8e91-c07fb47fab97"}